⭐ AWS Services Used (Explained Simply)

Below is EXACTLY how to explain in interviews.

🔶 1. AWS VPC (Virtual Private Cloud)
Why used?

To isolate our environment and keep backend + database secure.

What we created:

Public Subnet → EC2 + Load Balancer

Private Subnet → RDS Database

Internet Gateway → For internet access

Route Tables → Public & private routing

How it works in project:

Frontend and backend EC2 instances sit in public subnet.

RDS database sits in private subnet, not accessible from internet.

(Interview point: “Keeping RDS in a private subnet increases security.”)

🔶 2. AWS EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud)
Why used?

To run the backend application.

How implemented:

One EC2 instance runs the Docker container of backend app.

EC2 pulls Docker image from DockerHub automatically in deployment.

EC2 has security groups allowing only:

ALB → port 80

RDS → port 3306

🔶 3. AWS RDS (Relational Database Service)
Why used?

To store expense data securely.

What we used:

MySQL/PostgreSQL DB instance

Multi-AZ (optional)

Automated backups

Usage in project:

Backend connects to RDS using:

DB_HOST=myproject-db.xxxxxxxxx.rds.amazonaws.com
USERNAME=admin
PASSWORD=*****


Tables:

expenses (
   id INT PRIMARY KEY AUTO_INCREMENT,
   title VARCHAR(255),
   amount FLOAT,
   category VARCHAR(100),
   date DATE
)

🔶 4. AWS S3 (Simple Storage Service)
Why used?

To store:

Static files (CSS, JS, images)

Expense receipts (if uploaded)

Implementation:

Created S3 bucket: expense-app-static-bucket

Enabled versioning

Public access disabled (only through CloudFront or signed URLs if needed)

🔶 5. AWS Load Balancer (Application Load Balancer)
Why used?

For:

High availability

Routing traffic to EC2 backend

How used:

ALB forwards HTTP traffic on port 80 to EC2 instance

Health checks ensure backend is healthy

🔶 6. AWS IAM (Identity & Access Management)
Why used?

To securely access AWS services.

IAM roles used:

EC2 role → pull objects from S3

Jenkins role → deploy to EC2, S3, RDS

Policies:

AmazonEC2FullAccess

AmazonS3FullAccess

RDSFullAccess (limited)

CloudWatchLogsFullAccess

⭐ CI/CD Pipeline (Jenkins, Docker, SonarCloud)
