⭐ Logic Behind the Project – Explained Simply

This is EXACTLY how to explain it:

🔷 1. Expense Creation Logic (Add Expense)

When a user adds an expense:

Input from user:

Title → "Lunch"

Amount → 200

Category → "Food"

Date → "2025-02-01"

Backend Logic:

Validate inputs

Create an expense object

Insert into RDS database

Database entry (example):
id	title	amount	category	date
1	Lunch	200	Food	2025-02-01
🔷 2. View Expenses Logic

When user clicks “View Expenses”:

Backend performs:

SELECT * FROM expenses ORDER BY date DESC;


Returns list of expenses → Shown on frontend.

🔷 3. Update Expense Logic

When user edits an expense:

User selects record

Enters new values

Backend updates row using:

UPDATE expenses
SET title=?, amount=?, category=?, date=?
WHERE id=?

🔷 4. Delete Expense Logic

User clicks delete.

Backend executes:

DELETE FROM expenses WHERE id=?;


The row gets removed.

🔷 5. Monthly Total Logic

To find total for a month:

SELECT SUM(amount)
FROM expenses
WHERE MONTH(date)=1 AND YEAR(date)=2025;


Returns:

✔ Total monthly spending → shown in dashboard

🔷 6. Category-wise Spending Logic

To generate pie chart/summary:

SELECT category, SUM(amount)
FROM expenses
GROUP BY category;


Returns:

Food → 1200

Travel → 800

Shopping → 500

